{"id":"NCT07558590","title":"RETRO-PROSPECTIVE POSTMARKET CLINICAL STUDY FOR FX SHOULDER SOLUTIONS SHOULDER SYSTEMS","official":"RETRO-PROSPECTIVE POSTMARKET CLINICAL STUDY FOR FX SHOULDER SOLUTIONS SHOULDER SYSTEMS","summary":"This study takes place in the framework of the PostMarket Clinical Follow-up plan of the Shoulder Systems commercialized by FX SHOULDER SOLUTIONS.\n\nThe included cases will be followed for 10 years after index surgery. Primary objective is the assessment in real life of the revision rate of the shoulder systems at long-term.\n\nSecondary objectives are\n\n* Revision rate at each post op visit\n* Range of motion at each post op visit\n* Quick Dash, Constant, American Shoulder and Elbow Surgeons Shoulder Score (ASES), Subjective Shoulder Value (SSV), Pain scores at each post op visit\n* Radiological assessment of implant positioning through geometrical parameters at each post op visit\n* Incidence of complications at each post op visit\n* Qualitative feedback from surgeons on the instrumentation","conditions":["Humeral Fracture, Proximal","Glenohumeral Osteoarthritis","Avascular Necrosis of the Head of Humerus","Rotator Cuff Tear","Rotator Cuff Arthropathy","Inflammatory Arthritis","Revision of a Shoulder Prosthesis"],"interventions":[{"type":"PROCEDURE","name":"Shoulder arthroplasty"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Indication for hemi or total shoulder replacement with one of the FX SHOULDER SOLUTIONS Shoulder Systems, according to its IFU and surgical technique.\n* Patient aged 18 years and above\n* Patient insured with a social security system\n* Has been informed and did consent to participate to the study.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Neurological pathologies compromising the shoulder stability\n* Morbid obesity\n* Muscular deficiencies impairing the shoulder joint","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":1004,"start":"2020-06-01","pcd":"2036-12-31","upd":"2026-04-30","sponsor":"FX Solutions","areas":["other","rare"],"central":["Kathy TRIER, PhD · 800-280-0775 · ktrier@fxshouldersolutions.com","Gabriel GUEUGNON · ggueugnon@fxshouldersolutions.com"],"sites":[{"f":"CHU Amiens Picardie","city":"Amiens","pr":"","zip":"80054","s":"R","lat":49.9,"lon":2.3,"c":"david.emmanuel@chu-amiens.fr"},{"f":"CHU d' Angers","city":"Angers","pr":"","zip":"49933","s":"R","lat":47.4716,"lon":-0.552,"c":"LANCIGU, MD · romain.lancigu@gmail.com"},{"f":"Hôpital Jean Minjoz","city":"Besançon","pr":"","zip":"25030","s":"R","lat":47.2488,"lon":6.0182,"c":"OBERT, Pr, MD · laurentobert@yahoo.fr"},{"f":"Clinique Aguiléra","city":"Biarritz","pr":"","zip":"64200","s":"R","lat":43.4806,"lon":-1.5568,"c":"LEGER, MD"},{"f":"Hôpital privé Saint-Martin","city":"Caen","pr":"","zip":"14000","s":"R","lat":49.1859,"lon":-0.3591,"c":"DORDAIN, MD · fdordain@gmail.com"},{"f":"Infirmerie Protestante","city":"Caluire-et-Cuire","pr":"","zip":"69300","s":"R","lat":45.7946,"lon":4.8464,"c":"Thierry AUTHOM, MD · +33 4.72.00.71.60 · thierry.authom@infirmerie-protestante.com"},{"f":"CHMS Chambéry","city":"Chambéry","pr":"","zip":"73011","s":"R","lat":45.5663,"lon":5.9208,"c":"Emmanuel BEAUDOUIN, MD · +33 4.79.96.51.44 · Emmanuel.Beaudouin@ch-metropole-savoie.fr"},{"f":"HÔPITAUX CIVILS de Colmar","city":"Colmar","pr":"","zip":"68024","s":"R","lat":48.0808,"lon":7.3558,"c":"ROBIAL, MD · fdordain@gmail.com"},{"f":"Hôpital privé Dijon Bourgogne","city":"Dijon","pr":"","zip":"21000","s":"R","lat":47.3134,"lon":5.0139,"c":"GONZALVEZ, MD · mgonzalvez@orthopedie-du-parc.fr"},{"f":"Clinique Saint Charles","city":"La Roche-sur-Yon","pr":"","zip":"85016","s":"R","lat":46.6697,"lon":-1.4276,"c":"HEIZMANN, MD · jheizmann.csc@sa3h.fr"},{"f":"Clinique chirurgicale Porte Océane","city":"Les Sables-d'Olonne","pr":"","zip":"85101","s":"R","lat":46.4969,"lon":-1.7847,"c":"MARCHAND, MD · drjbmarchand@gmail.com"},{"f":"Clinique Saint Charles","city":"Lyon","pr":"","zip":"69001","s":"R","lat":45